---- MODULE Quicksort ----
EXTENDS Naturals, Sequences

CONSTANTS Values, MaxSeqLen

\* Sequence positions are 1-indexed here, but the partitioning transformation
\* itself is index-free: it only relates values before and after the step.
Indices == 1..MaxSeqLen
Domain == [Indices -> Values \cup {0}]
Subseq(s, i, j) == [k \in i..j |-> s[k]]

VARIABLES seq, original, work, pc
vars == <<seq, original, work, pc>>

TypeOK ==
    /\ seq \in Domain
    /\ original \in Domain
    /\ work \subseteq (Indices \X Indices)
    /\ pc \in {"running", "done"}

Init ==
    \E s \in [Indices -> Values] :
        /\ seq = s
        /\ original = s
        /\ work = {<<1, MaxSeqLen>>}
        /\ pc = "running"

\* Permutations are generated by name rather than enumerated, because a
\* nondeterministic partition can produce any permutation satisfying the
\* relation below; enumerating them would be exactly what the model tries to
\* avoid.  Bounded Model Checking (with MaxSeqLen) keeps this from running away.
Permutations(p) ==
    {q \in [Indices -> Values] :
        /\ \A k \in Indices : (k < p \/ k > MaxSeqLen) => q[k] = seq[k]
        /\ \A i, j \in 1..MaxSeqLen :
              (i <= p /\ j <= p) => (seq[i] = seq[j] <=> q[i] = q[j])
        /\ \A i, j \in 1..MaxSeqLen :
              (i > p /\ j > p) => (seq[i] = seq[j] <=> q[i] = q[j])
        /\ \A i, j \in 1..MaxSeqLen :
              (i <= p /\ j > p) => q[i] <= q[j]
        /\ \A i, j \in 1..MaxSeqLen :
              (i > p /\ j <= p) => q[j] <= q[i]}

IsPermutation(s) ==
    /\ \A x \in Values : \A i, j \in 1..MaxSeqLen :
          (s[i] = x /\ s[j] = x) => (i = j <=> original[i] = original[j])
    /\ \A i \in 1..MaxSeqLen : original[i] # 0 => s[i] # 0

\* The sortedness relation is per-interval: the intervals in the work set are
\* pairwise-disjoint, and every interval is internally non-decreasing, which
\* together imply the whole sequence is sorted once the work set is empty.
Sorted ==
    \A i, j \in 1..MaxSeqLen :
        /\ i <= j => seq[i] <= seq[j]
        /\ (seq[i] = 0 <=> seq[j] = 0)

IntervalSorted(i, j) ==
    \A x, y \in i..j : seq[x] <= seq[y]

\* The invariant is a conjunction of three things, so it is not replaceable.
Inv ==
    /\ \A i, j \in Indices :
         <<i, j>> \in work => IntervalSorted(i, j)
    /\ IsPermutation(seq)
    /\ \A i, j, k, l \in Indices :
         (<<i, j>> \in work /\ <<k, l>> \in work /\ i <= k) => (k > j \/ i <= k <= j /\ j <= l)

Partition ==
    \/ \E s \in Permutations(MaxSeqLen) : seq' = s
    /\ seq' # seq

SortStep ==
    /\ pc = "running"
    /\ \E int \in work :
        /\ work' = work \ {int}
        /\ IF int[1] = int[2] THEN UNCHANGED seq
           ELSE /\ \E p \in int[1]..(int[2] - 1) :
                    /\ Partition
                    /\ work' = work' \cup {<<int[1], p>>, <<p + 1, int[2]>>}
    /\ pc' = IF work' = {} THEN "done" ELSE pc

Next == SortStep \/ (pc = "done" /\ UNCHANGED vars)

Spec ==
    /\ Init
    /\ [][Next]_vars
    /\ WF_vars(SortStep)

PCorrect == (pc = "done") => Sorted

\* The transformation is never stuck once work is empty: termination is
\* reachable from every reachable state.
Termination == <>(pc = "done")

\* Bounded model checking of the full permutation space is not meant to run
\* forever, so a per-step finite bound on shuffled values keeps it checkable.
LimitedSeq == Seq

====